      "writtenOn": "2021-08-18T09:53:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Where in this CL `data` is causing a readability problem?\n\nI had to check twice when reading changes.\n- why \"Debug\" is removed for this? while other structs are still \"Debug\"..\n- why write_into should have self as mut? In general, write functions don\u0027t require the data as mutable. (like write_into of HashingInfo and SigningInfo)\n\nThe type itself is not straightforward as well: V4Signature\u003cR: Read + Seek\u003e. In general, we don\u0027t expect that \"signature\" of something depends on \"Read+Seek\".",
      "parentUuid": "e39cfcfb_c03746b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 4,
